WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.398 --> 00:00:01.343
- It's so crazy not knowing

00:00:01.343 --> 00:00:05.093
what's getting tattooed
to my body right now.

00:00:08.048 --> 00:00:09.575
- We're here about to get tattoos.

00:00:09.575 --> 00:00:11.305
I've no idea what she's picked for me,

00:00:11.305 --> 00:00:12.588
and vice versa.

00:00:12.588 --> 00:00:14.231
It's a little bit nerve wracking.

00:00:14.231 --> 00:00:15.559
- It's tormenting.

00:00:15.559 --> 00:00:17.784
- (Together) We're getting married!

00:00:17.784 --> 00:00:18.997
- We getting married.

00:00:18.997 --> 00:00:20.460
- We are engaged,

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:22.910
and we've been together
for more than a year.

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:24.442
- We've known each
other since high school.

00:00:24.442 --> 00:00:25.475
- For about 11 years.

00:00:25.475 --> 00:00:26.984
We both packed up our lives

00:00:26.984 --> 00:00:28.784
and shipped over here from Sydney.

00:00:28.784 --> 00:00:30.607
So that took a great deal of trust.

00:00:30.607 --> 00:00:32.813
- I feel like this is
the ultimate trust test

00:00:32.813 --> 00:00:34.206
before the wedding.

00:00:34.206 --> 00:00:38.502
- I'm still nervous, but this
is like nothing in comparison.

00:00:38.502 --> 00:00:41.451
It's her body, and suddenly
I have this weird authority

00:00:41.451 --> 00:00:44.580
over it, which is really
uncomfortable, to be honest.

00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:46.941
- I'm hoping I really love this tattoo,

00:00:46.941 --> 00:00:49.326
because I'm going to be
walking down the aisle

00:00:49.326 --> 00:00:50.743
with this tattoo.

00:00:52.432 --> 00:00:54.515
(laughs)

00:01:00.305 --> 00:01:01.423
- Hey Mike, Rachelle.

00:01:01.423 --> 00:01:02.256
- Nice to meet you.

00:01:02.256 --> 00:01:03.094
- How are you?

00:01:03.094 --> 00:01:04.230
- You're picking something
for your girlfriend,

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:05.129
what are you thinking?

00:01:05.129 --> 00:01:07.175
- I'm actually thinking of this leaf.

00:01:07.175 --> 00:01:09.269
The gum leaf from back home in Australia.

00:01:09.269 --> 00:01:12.777
We're really hungover just
drawing on bits of garden.

00:01:12.777 --> 00:01:14.534
That was a leaf that I drew.

00:01:14.534 --> 00:01:15.367
- Oh, that's cool.

00:01:15.367 --> 00:01:16.808
- And she was like,
I'm keeping it forever.

00:01:16.808 --> 00:01:18.650
And she was like stoked on this one.

00:01:18.650 --> 00:01:20.764
She actually lost it later that day,

00:01:20.764 --> 00:01:22.297
her housemate put it in the bin.

00:01:22.297 --> 00:01:23.464
The next morning I woke up,

00:01:23.464 --> 00:01:24.682
and I could hear all this stuff

00:01:24.682 --> 00:01:26.053
outside the back of the house,

00:01:26.053 --> 00:01:28.909
and she was actually
emptying a full garbage bin,

00:01:28.909 --> 00:01:30.957
and she found it and kept it.

00:01:30.957 --> 00:01:32.148
And she still has it.

00:01:32.148 --> 00:01:35.143
That's a little cool reminder
of finding her in the trash.

00:01:35.143 --> 00:01:37.010
- I actually have two ideas as well,

00:01:37.010 --> 00:01:40.047
depending on what is
viable for the timeframe.

00:01:40.047 --> 00:01:42.724
I found this picture of a pomegranate.

00:01:42.724 --> 00:01:44.524
Every time I see them, I think of her,

00:01:44.524 --> 00:01:46.641
but I also think of my
culture and heritage.

00:01:46.641 --> 00:01:47.474
What do you think?

00:01:47.474 --> 00:01:48.576
- Let's take a look at the other one.

00:01:48.576 --> 00:01:52.242
- So when Rachelle and
I first started dating.

00:01:52.242 --> 00:01:53.075
- Really?

00:01:53.075 --> 00:01:54.781
- And this was one of the leaves.

00:01:54.781 --> 00:01:56.584
- Let me take a peek at that.

00:01:56.584 --> 00:01:58.768
- And my housemates actually
threw that leaf away,

00:01:58.768 --> 00:02:00.406
so I had to rummage in the bin.

00:02:00.406 --> 00:02:01.239
- Did you really?

00:02:01.239 --> 00:02:02.072
- To find it.

00:02:02.072 --> 00:02:04.841
It was covered in all sorts of things.

00:02:04.841 --> 00:02:05.944
- Here.

00:02:05.944 --> 00:02:07.406
(laughs)

00:02:07.406 --> 00:02:08.239
- I like it.

00:02:08.239 --> 00:02:09.072
It's a gum leaf?

00:02:09.072 --> 00:02:09.905
- Yeah, it's a gum leaf.

00:02:09.905 --> 00:02:10.738
And we're Australian.

00:02:10.738 --> 00:02:11.571
- I know my leaves.

00:02:11.571 --> 00:02:13.119
- I thought maybe the lines here

00:02:13.119 --> 00:02:16.293
would be a little bit too fine.

00:02:16.293 --> 00:02:17.641
- I have a feeling we
might be able to come up

00:02:17.641 --> 00:02:20.051
with a simpler version of this.

00:02:20.051 --> 00:02:22.134
That way, it can be done.

00:02:23.243 --> 00:02:25.472
- I think we should go pomegranate then.

00:02:25.472 --> 00:02:27.272
Simple, yet complicated.

00:02:27.272 --> 00:02:28.645
Just like her.

00:02:28.645 --> 00:02:31.074
The splash of red as well, is like fire.

00:02:31.074 --> 00:02:31.907
- Yes.

00:02:31.907 --> 00:02:32.989
- Love.

00:02:32.989 --> 00:02:34.489
Unbridled passion.

00:02:35.463 --> 00:02:37.036
She's so going to break up with me.

00:02:37.036 --> 00:02:38.340
- So what are you looking to get done?

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:39.416
On her, shall I say?

00:02:39.416 --> 00:02:40.982
- I think it would be really cool to have

00:02:40.982 --> 00:02:44.384
by grace, through faith tattooed on her.

00:02:44.384 --> 00:02:45.217
- Okay.

00:02:45.217 --> 00:02:46.298
- It comes from the Bible,

00:02:46.298 --> 00:02:48.906
and just encapsulates her journey.

00:02:48.906 --> 00:02:51.226
Went through some very
difficult times in our life,

00:02:51.226 --> 00:02:53.835
but her faith in Christ is
what kept her so strong.

00:02:53.835 --> 00:02:58.089
She loves super
minimalistic cursive fonts.

00:02:58.089 --> 00:03:01.506
- I was thinking of getting for the good,

00:03:02.455 --> 00:03:05.288
but in a nice, modern, clean font.

00:03:06.616 --> 00:03:10.913
And I'd like to make the
T kind of like a cross.

00:03:10.913 --> 00:03:11.746
Yeah.

00:03:11.746 --> 00:03:14.290
I feel like he's just such a warrior,

00:03:14.290 --> 00:03:17.148
his favorite verse is Romans 8:28,

00:03:17.148 --> 00:03:19.758
and it's all things work
together for the good.

00:03:19.758 --> 00:03:21.467
You know, things happen for a reason.

00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:23.944
I think that's just something he lives by,

00:03:23.944 --> 00:03:28.111
and I fell confidant that
it's something he will love.

00:03:29.251 --> 00:03:30.354
Ready to go!

00:03:30.354 --> 00:03:31.187
Wait, wait, wait.

00:03:31.187 --> 00:03:33.707
Can we sketch it out?

00:03:33.707 --> 00:03:35.596
- No, no, we just free hand it on.

00:03:35.596 --> 00:03:37.128
We don't use a stencil or anything.

00:03:37.128 --> 00:03:37.961
- Really?

00:03:37.961 --> 00:03:39.202
- No, yes, we'll sketch it out.

00:03:39.202 --> 00:03:40.119
- Oh, good.

00:03:53.478 --> 00:03:55.061
- [Tan] Here we go.

00:04:01.216 --> 00:04:02.504
- Ow!

00:04:02.504 --> 00:04:03.337
Okay!

00:04:15.239 --> 00:04:16.072
- [Charlie] It's okay, baby.

00:04:16.072 --> 00:04:17.750
- Sorry buddy, gotta stay on that side.

00:04:17.750 --> 00:04:18.583
- Why?

00:04:18.583 --> 00:04:21.058
- LA County Healthcare violation.

00:04:21.058 --> 00:04:22.835
Cheerleaders got to stay in the stands.

00:04:22.835 --> 00:04:25.835
- I just want to hold her hand, man!

00:04:32.159 --> 00:04:33.645
- We done.

00:04:33.645 --> 00:04:34.949
- Yeah.

00:04:34.949 --> 00:04:35.782
- Really?

00:04:39.310 --> 00:04:41.810
- [Man] Three, two, one, look.

00:04:47.239 --> 00:04:49.246
- For the good.

00:04:49.246 --> 00:04:50.414
(laughs)

00:04:50.414 --> 00:04:51.494
I love it.

00:04:51.494 --> 00:04:52.327
- Really?

00:04:52.327 --> 00:04:53.811
- Yeah.

00:04:53.811 --> 00:04:55.250
That's my favorite Bible verse.

00:04:55.250 --> 00:04:57.728
All things happen for the good.

00:04:57.728 --> 00:04:59.167
This verse has kept me through

00:04:59.167 --> 00:05:00.829
everything that I've been through.

00:05:00.829 --> 00:05:02.767
I held on to this truth,

00:05:02.767 --> 00:05:05.037
especially when it came to
who my future wife would be,

00:05:05.037 --> 00:05:07.875
and I just had this
incredible amount of faith,

00:05:07.875 --> 00:05:10.912
and He led me to you, which
is the greatest blessing.

00:05:10.912 --> 00:05:11.789
I love you.

00:05:11.789 --> 00:05:13.273
- I love you too.

00:05:13.273 --> 00:05:15.773
- [Man] Three, two, one, look.

00:05:18.313 --> 00:05:20.063
- Aw, it's so pretty!

00:05:22.789 --> 00:05:24.033
I love it!

00:05:24.033 --> 00:05:24.866
- [Charlie] You love it?

00:05:24.866 --> 00:05:25.699
- Yes!

00:05:25.699 --> 00:05:27.872
Thank you so much!

00:05:27.872 --> 00:05:30.974
It says by grace, through faith

00:05:30.974 --> 00:05:34.037
in the most pretty cursive writing.

00:05:34.037 --> 00:05:38.204
I'm obsessed with like little,
cursive writing like this.

00:05:39.685 --> 00:05:41.102
- Yeah!

00:05:41.102 --> 00:05:43.598
- Thank you, I love it.

00:05:43.598 --> 00:05:44.681
- I love you.

00:05:49.652 --> 00:05:52.152
- [Man] Three, two, one, look.

00:05:55.615 --> 00:05:56.948
- A pomegranate!

00:05:58.403 --> 00:06:00.968
I thought it was really
round, like a crab.

00:06:00.968 --> 00:06:02.205
- Well, it is.

00:06:02.205 --> 00:06:03.038
It is.

00:06:05.490 --> 00:06:06.773
Do you like it?

00:06:06.773 --> 00:06:08.392
- Yeah.

00:06:08.392 --> 00:06:09.225
Holy crap.

00:06:10.843 --> 00:06:12.462
I didn't even think of that.

00:06:12.462 --> 00:06:13.295
- That's kind of like you,

00:06:13.295 --> 00:06:15.324
because it's like a little bit gory,

00:06:15.324 --> 00:06:19.623
and the veins remind me of a
heart, like it's anatomical.

00:06:19.623 --> 00:06:21.648
This represents you to me.

00:06:21.648 --> 00:06:23.088
- It fits really well.

00:06:23.088 --> 00:06:25.428
- I thought so too, thank you so much.

00:06:25.428 --> 00:06:26.845
I did good, guys.

00:06:28.786 --> 00:06:32.939
- It felt like a whole bunch
of zig-zagging at one point.

00:06:32.939 --> 00:06:34.332
Like an octopus.

00:06:34.332 --> 00:06:36.427
- [Man] Three, two, one, look.

00:06:36.427 --> 00:06:37.427
- Oh my god.

00:06:38.296 --> 00:06:39.129
Oh my god!

00:06:43.021 --> 00:06:43.854
Woah!

00:06:45.089 --> 00:06:47.788
I was going to get you that!

00:06:47.788 --> 00:06:49.365
- I thought that, I thought you might,

00:06:49.365 --> 00:06:51.028
so that's why I was freaking out.

00:06:51.028 --> 00:06:51.861
- Amazing.

00:06:53.390 --> 00:06:55.473
Aw, Rickie, it's so cute.

00:06:56.966 --> 00:06:58.475
That's so amazing.

00:06:58.475 --> 00:07:01.018
It's a leaf that I will
keep with me forever now.

00:07:01.018 --> 00:07:02.481
And I said to her.

00:07:02.481 --> 00:07:03.763
I was like, this leaf is staying

00:07:03.763 --> 00:07:07.930
with me forever, at the
time, and now it really is.

